# CODEOWNERS — who is automatically asked to review changes to which files.
#
# Two developers, both named directly. With "required approvals: 1" on the main
# ruleset, the other person already reviews everything; this file only adds the
# paths where the WRONG person reviewing would be a real loss, so that a review
# request is raised automatically for them.
#
# On this public repository CODEOWNERS is enforced by the ruleset. If a third
# person ever joins, revisit — see ops/github-setup.md in the docs repository.

# Default: either developer may review anything.
*                               @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hot files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# components/polilingo.tsx is 41 KB and app/globals.css is 71 KB. Both are
# touched by almost every feature, so with two people working in parallel they
# are where merge conflicts come from. Splitting them is week-1 work. Until
# that lands, the hot-file protocol in process/how-we-work.md (docs repository)
# applies: say in the daily message that you are going into one of these, keep
# the change small, and merge the same day.

/components/polilingo.tsx       @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006
/app/globals.css                @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Things that are expensive to get wrong
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Learning state. lib/progress.ts decides XP, streaks and what is unlocked, and
# its anti-double-award logic is subtle. It is also the data that has to migrate
# into accounts without destroying anyone's streak. Changes here need a second
# pair of eyes and a test.
/lib/progress.ts                @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006
/tests/                         @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006

